# Forked from Alpine's main/mesa (aports master, 26.2.6-r0, 2026-11-05) for
# amazon-suez only: Mesa main (11-17, which has !42747, the pco preamble, since
# 11-12 as 40198eca3db; our 0001 copy of it is dropped) and local
# PowerVR prototypes that make the Phosh desktop GPU-accelerated on the
# GX6250 (phoc's frame 84 -> 16 ms). The patches come from ~/repos/mesa
# branch suez/pvr-desktop-pkg and are LOCAL EXPERIMENTS, NEVER TO BE SENT:
# Imagination declines LLM-generated code in src/imagination. Evidence:
# suez-work notes/PVR-DESKTOP-2026-11-04.md; book GPU chapter. 0020 (r2):
# suez-work notes/PLASMA-LOCKSCREEN-REDRAW-2026-11-14.md §6. 0021 (r3): same
# note, §11 (window-sized images stored linearly: ~155 MB less pinned);
# 0022 (r3): transfer submit scratch kept per context (task switcher).
# 0023-0024 (r4): the suballocator keeps up to eight emptied buffers, and the
# render target cache holds 32 sizes: Plasma's drawers stop creating kernel
# buffers every frame (action drawer close 48-64 -> 32 ms per frame).
# 0025 (r5): only 32-bit formats take 0021's linear rule; linear R8 images
# sampled wrong (Firefox's software-decoded video at half size, rest garbled).
# 0026 (r6): the SPM end-of-tile shader shares 0016's cache; it was
# compiled on every vkCmdBeginRendering, ~1.1 ms of CPU per render pass
# (notes/MARQUEE-COST-2026-11-16.md in suez-work).
# 0027 (r7): maxTexelBufferElements 64Ki -> 8192 x 4096; with 64Ki the GL
# state tracker refused its GPU PBO upload for anything larger and copied
# on the CPU, waiting for the GPU (Firefox's video planes;
# notes/BROWSER-PERF-2026-11-16.md in suez-work).
# 0028 (r8): pco checks only src1 for NaN in NaN-preserving fmin/fmax
# (min/max already return src1 for a NaN src0); every GLSL clamp() pays
# this since 7e22c43f658; Firefox's YUV pass 15.9 -> 13.1 ms.
# 0029 (r9): pco commutes fadd/fmul/fmad sources instead of copying a
# uniform out of S1 with a mov group per use (Firefox shaders -4.5 %,
# Angelfish's -8 %, bit-exact).
# 0030 (r10): pco folds a constant LOD bias into the sampler's own bias
# (computed in the preamble) instead of passing it per pixel; biased samples
# cost the texture unit ~2.5x. Skia biases by -0.475: Angelfish's 720p video
# compositor pass 27 -> 6.4 ms, dropped frames 12.4 -> 0 per second.
# 0031+0032 (r11): pvr passes raw single-channel transfer copies through
# instead of clamping and packing four channels, and pco takes gl_FragCoord
# from the pixel registers in pixel-rate transfer shaders: the R8 copy
# shader 31 -> 5 instruction groups; a 1280x720 R8 upload (video Y plane)
# 2.6 -> 1.1 ms of GPU time (notes/XFER-2026-11-17.md in suez-work).
# 0033+0034 (r12): the DRM winsys submitted only the first prepare of a
# multi-pass transfer, and a prepare with two clip rectangles (two PBE
# render targets) wrote garbage or page-faulted on GX6250: copies with an
# odd row length and odd height (e.g. glReadPixels of a 203x117 image) were
# wrong or faulted. Every prepare is now a job, one clip rectangle per pass.
# 0035 (r13): 0018's default preamble stays off for compute shaders: a
# compute shader sampling a texture page-faulted the compute data master
# with it (PCO_DEBUG=preamble still enables it there).
# r14 / 27.0.0_git20261117: rebased onto Mesa main 01638af585b (11-17); 0001
# (!42747) dropped as merged and reused for a LOCAL revert of Mesa's
# wayland-protocols 1.50 requirement (Alpine edge has 1.49); 0002-0035
# unchanged in content (applied without conflict); tested on the board like r13 (suez-work notes/MESA-REBASE-2026-11-17.md).
#
# Trimmed to what suez uses: gallium zink and llvmpipe, Vulkan imagination
# and lavapipe; no VA, no rusticl, no Vulkan layers. Do not merge this into
# pmaports master.
